# What must not reach the build context.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter. `data/` is 80 MB of DuckDB
# plus, in `data/custody/`, other people's encrypted ESPN sessions -- neither
# belongs in an image layer, and the custody file least of all: image layers
# are cached, pushed to a registry and generally treated as public within an
# organisation. It arrives on the mounted volume instead. `.env` is the key
# that makes that file readable, so the two of them in one image would undo
# the entire point of encrypting it.

data/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Built by the web stage inside the image, never copied from the host: a
# stale local build would otherwise win over the one just compiled.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Development and research surface with no runtime role.
tests/
docs/
design/
research/
scripts/
.claude/
.superpowers/
.design/
.playwright-mcp/
*.patch
*.out
README.md
Makefile
